// ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1 v1.1, the N16R8 ordering.
// Schematic: SCH_ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1_V1.1_20221130, sheet 02, rev V1.1.
// Header names: ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1 v1.1 User Guide, Header Block, J1 and J3.
// That section says the numbering matches the Board Schematic and links
// SCH_ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1_V1.1_20220413.pdf. Related Documents names the
// 20221130 sheet this part uses. The pin names below are the Header Block.
// The user guide says v1.1 drives the RGB LED from GPIO38. v1.0 used GPIO48.
//
// J2 is the USB-UART socket. Its VBUS is the 5 V rail. The sheet puts a
// 1N5819HW-7-F (D1) between that VBUS and VCC_5V. The catalog diode is a
// different part, so the wire is straight and D1 is not placed. J4, the
// module's USB socket, has the same diode (D7) onto VCC_5V. Each socket is
// an ideal 5 V source, so J4's VBUS is not joined onto that rail.
// R7, R8, R9, R13 and R17 are 0 ohm, 1%, and resistor-0603 cannot be 0, so
// each is a wire. R24, the sheet's 0 ohm on the module's 3V3 feed, is the
// wire from the regulator output to the module.
// The sheet also shows R11 5.1k and D5, the red power LED, C6 1 uF on
// CHIP_PU, R16 1k on the bridge RSTb, R14 10k marked NC, C13, C14 and C15
// marked NC, and R19 22.1k with R18 47.5k and C12 1 uF on the bridge VBUS
// pin. None of those is placed: the chip model has no reset pin, and the
// bridge model does not read RSTb or VBUS. The populated rail capacitors
// on VCC_3V3 (C1, C2, C9, C10, C11) and VCC_5V (C3, C7, C8) are placed.
