  // Copper centres from DXF_ESP32-S3-DevKitC-1_V1.1_20220429, PADLAYER_TOP,
  // shifted so the outline centre (12.7, 31.4325) is the origin. The outline
  // polyline is x = 0 to 25.40 and y = 0 to 62.865. Antenna is +Y. z is the
  // board thickness in model.py, which that drawing does not state.
  // mod is the module body centre (12.75, 56.39): side lands at x = 4.0 and
  // 21.5, pin 1 at y = 61.65 (7.49 from the antenna end), bottom row at
  // y = 43.89 (0.25 inside the far end). Figure 11-1 of the module datasheet.
  // j1 and j3 are the header lands, x = 1.27 and 24.13, y = 61.3 down to
  // 7.96. Pin 1 is the antenna end, so each header's -X lead turns to +Y.
  // j2 and j4 are the centres of the four shell lands, (6.0, 3.66233) and
  // (19.4, 3.66233). The catalog micro-B marks its sizes "verify", and its
  // pad row does not sit on this connector's five signal lands (y = 4.967,
  // pitch 0.65). The mouth points off the board.
  // bridge is the 3.25 exposed pad at (13.589, 20.1422). The DXF does not
  // number those leads. Leaving it unturned puts the model's pin 1 at the
  // +Y end of the -X edge.
  // ldo: three 2.0 by 1.5 lands at x = 10.3378 on a 2.3 pitch, the middle
  // one at y = 36.3728. A half turn points the tab toward the 2.0 by 3.8
  // land at x = 16.638. That land's centre is not the model's tab centre.
  // The copper does not mark pin 1.
  // q1 and q2 are the midpoint of the collector land and the other pair.
  // Q1's collector is (17.780, 30.23311) and the pair is at y = 27.93289.
  // Q2's collector is (12.573, 30.23311). The pair lands are 1.9 apart.
  // The part's e is 0.95.
  // led is the centre of the four 1.0 by 1.5 lands, (7.493, 29.083). The
  // longer pitch runs along Y, so the 3.7 mm side turns to Y. The copper
  // does not mark pin 1. The land pitch is 1.8 by 3.3. The part's pad
  // centres are 2.78 by 1.78.
  // sw_boot and sw_reset are the centres of the four 1.05 by 0.65 lands,
  // (7.5254, 13.9586) and (17.9054, 13.9586). The X pitch is 4.15, which
  // matches the model. The Y pitch on the land is 2.15. The model's row
  // pitch is 2.8.
  // The diodes are the centre of each 0.40 by 0.48 pair. The length runs
  // along Y. The copper does not mark the cathode. Left to right the pairs
  // are D2, D3, D4 and D8, D9, D10.
  // r_en, r_dtr and r_rts are the centres of the 0.508 squares under R5,
  // R10 and R12, 1.016 apart. Those lands are smaller than this 0603. The
  // sheet prints 10K(1%) and does not name the body. Length along X.
  // c1, c3, c7, c10 and c11 are the centres of the 0.8 by 0.9 mm 0603 lands
  // on a 1.65 mm pitch (C1 runs along Y; C3, C7, C10 and C11 run along X).
  // c2, c8 and c9 are the centres of the 0.508 squares on a 1.016 pitch
  // running along Y; those lands are smaller than this 0603.
