  "not_simulated": [
    { "what": "RST", "pins": ["RST"], "why": "J1 pin 3 is EN, the chip's CHIP_PU. The esp32s3 kind has no reset pin. The sheet's truth table for DTR and RTS still wires Q1 and Q2, and the model does not reset when EN moves." },
    { "what": "GPIO35, GPIO36 and GPIO37", "pins": ["GPIO35", "GPIO36", "GPIO37"], "why": "The user guide says that on an octal-SPI WROOM module these three pins are used inside the module and are not available. J3 still brings them out, as the header table lists them." },
    { "what": "the second USB 5 V", "why": "J2 and J4 are each an ideal 5 V host. The sheet diode-ORs them onto VCC_5V through 1N5819HW-7-F parts D1 and D7. That diode is not the catalog diode, so only J2's VBUS feeds the regulator and the 5V pin. J4's VBUS stays on its own net. J4 D- and D+ still go to GPIO19 and GPIO20." },
    { "what": "parts the sheet shows and this board does not place", "why": "R11 5.1k and D5, the red power LED. C6 1 uF on CHIP_PU (the reset delay capacitor), C12 1 uF with R19 22.1k and R18 47.5k on the bridge VBUS pin, R16 1k from the bridge RSTb to 3.3 V, and the parts marked NC (R14 10k, C13 0.1 uF, C14 0.1 uF, C15 10 uF). The bridge model does not read RSTb or VBUS. R7, R8, R9, R13, R17 and R24 are 0 ohm links and are wires." }
  ]
}
